# Tech stack lock

Use this stack. Do not add NestJS, a second backend, microservices, BullMQ, always-on workers, or WebSocket servers.

| Layer | Choice |
| --- | --- |
| App | Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript 5.9 `strict` |
| UI | Tailwind 4, shadcn/ui, lucide-react, next-themes, sonner |
| Forms | React Hook Form + Zod 4 |
| Client data | Apollo Client 4; Zustand only for real client UI state |
| API | GraphQL Yoga 5 + GraphQL 16 at `app/api/graphql/route.ts` (`/api/graphql`). Do not bump GraphQL to 17 until Yoga supports it. |
| DB | Prisma 7 + PostgreSQL (Neon). Driver adapter `@prisma/adapter-pg`. Client generated to `generated/prisma`. Config in `prisma.config.ts`. No local filesystem storage. |
| Files | Cloudflare R2 via `lib/storage` abstraction |
| Email | Resend via `lib/email` abstraction (never call Resend from domain services) |
| Payments | Stripe test mode; **webhooks are source of truth** |
| Jobs | Vercel Cron + DB state (`app/api/cron/*`), secret-protected, idempotent |
| Auth edge | `proxy.ts` at repo root exporting `proxy`. **Not** `middleware.ts`. |
| Deploy | Vercel serverless. Sessions in DB/cookies, not in-memory. |

## Allowed optional infra

- Upstash Redis only when a measured need exists (rate limit, cache). Never for basic CRUD.
- Sentry-compatible logging abstraction. No secrets in client bundles.

## Forbidden

```ts
// ❌ BAD
export function middleware(req: NextRequest) {}  // Next.js 16: use proxy.ts
writeFileSync("./uploads/x.pdf", buf)            // use R2
new Worker() / BullMQ / ws.Server()              // not Vercel-compatible

// ✅ GOOD
export function proxy(request: NextRequest) {}
await storage.upload({ key, body, mimeType })
```

Prefer fewer dependencies. Add a package only when the feature cannot be done with the stack above. Env vars live in `.env.example`; never commit `.env`.

Stay on **latest stable within this stack**. Do not bump to GraphQL 17 (Yoga 5 peers `^15 || ^16`), TypeScript 7 (Prisma 7 recommends 5.9.x), or ESLint 10 until `eslint-config-next` documents it. Prisma client is imported from `@/generated/prisma/client`, never `@prisma/client` directly.
